ter  not to mention he had the part at age 20  which made him the youngest actor to get  the role for once the character actually  felt like a high schooler as an added  bonus Pollan gave Peter a bit of a New  York accent Garfield did too but this  one feels the most like he's just a kid  from Queens Thank You mr. stark  I'm good Shameka more voices Miles  Morales a character who first put on the  spider-man mask an ultimate fallout  number four in 2011 since then  Morales has become a fan favorite and  fans have been begging for a movie for  years is it fair to judge Myles versus  the other versions of spider-man with  Peter Parker under the mask I say why  not though we only have a voice  performance to go off of more ends up  being a great choice he proves to be an  incredibly convincing high schooler  how many much body people are there next  let's talk about the movies themselves  there were a lot of things outside the  fight scenes that gave the original  trilogy an added dose of drama and say  what you will about the third movie but  the trilogy works together to build a  fascinating portrait of a character  split between power and responsibility  this great power comes great  responsibility  in the first movie Peter Parker's  unrequited love for Mary Jane is a big  highlight the tension of MJ liking  spider-man who can forget that  upside-down kiss while being just  friends with Peter added a special sense  of intrigue outside of the main action  in the second movie Peter looks like a  bad friend and nephew every time he has  to run out to be the hero he bears the  burden of being spider-man all alone  spider-man in spider-man 2 were at the  core about Peter Parker learning to  balance standing for justice and his  commitments to those he cared about in  his life by the end of the second movie  Mary Jane knows that Peter is spider-man  but in the third movie that knowledge  becomes a problem  Peter recreates that famous case with  Gwen Stacy and now Mary Jane clearly  sees the moments that Peter chooses hero  work over her which pushes her briefly  into the arms of Peters one-time best  friend Harry Osborn Harry is interesting  because like Mary Jane he learns about  Peters alter-ego but it causes him to  hate his old friend because spider-man  killed his father though spider-man 3 is  connected to the other two on a  character level overall it goes pretty  off the rails emo Spidey was a choice  and overall it just has too much going  on which will become a problem in the  next spider-man reboot  Garfield's movies have less of a  connecting thread the films work best  when they're taking a different  direction than the earlier trilogy but  ultimately it's too similar for a new  series with hardly any time separating  it from the earlier version this version  rehashes Uncle Ben's death Peter faces  off against the same bully at school  Harry's his best friend who turns into a  villain and he's pretty much battling  the same problems and demons but like I  said when it's different it's better in  this version Gwen Stacy who doesn't show  up until spider-man 3 in the first  version is Peters love interest Garfield  and Emma Stone have solid chemistry  another part that worked was giving more  of Peters early backstory by introducing  us to his parents but the filmmakers  were never able to shake off the  decision to retell spider-man's origin  story and didn't do enough to  differentiate Garfield spider-man while  McGuire's was still fresh in our minds  homecoming was smart and that it decide  to skip over spider-man's origin story  which we already seen twice on the big  screen it went right into where his  story left off following the events in  Germany from Civil War at the end of the  day everything about homecoming is fresh  he's a brand new love interest a new  funny best friend who's not named Harry  MJ comes as a surprise towards the end  of the movie and even his high school  bully flash is completely reimagined 